+    # Offset form: store the group minimum rather than a zero-point code.
+    #
+    # The original `zp = round(qmin - x_min/scale).clamp(qmin, qmax)` is wrong
+    # twice over. The clamp collapses any group that does not straddle zero
+    # (all-positive or all-negative), which post-RoPE keys hit constantly. And
+    # dropping the clamp is not enough either: EPS=1e-8 underflows to zero in
+    # the fp16 the scale is stored in, so a group whose spread falls below bf16
+    # resolution gets scale->0 and zp->inf, and dequantizing yields NaN.
+    #
+    # Storing x_min avoids both. It is a data value, so fp16 always holds it,
+    # and a constant group round-trips exactly (q=0 -> 0*scale + x_min).
+    # Storage cost is unchanged: one fp16 per group either way.
+    q = torch.round((x - x_min) / scale).clamp(qmin, qmax).to(torch.int8)
+    return q, scale.to(torch.float16), x_min.to(torch.float16)
 
 
